WEBVTT

1
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.391
If you must blink,
do it now.

2
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.636
Pay careful attention to
everything you see and hear,

3
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.119
no matter how unusual
it may seem.

4
00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.993
And please be warned,

5
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.393
if you fidget,
if you look away,

6
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.517
if you forget any part
of what I tell you,

7
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.556
even for an instant,

8
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.914
then our hero
will surely perish.

9
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.634
His name is Kubo.

10
00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.234
His grandfather
stole something from him.

11
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.028
And that really
is the least of it.

12
00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.480
Ow!

13
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.270
Well, hello, Kubo.

14
00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.793
How was it today?

15
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.838
It wasn't a bad crowd.

16
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.309
I got two pennies
and a lint ball.

17
00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.072
This is pretty good lint.

18
00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.512
And what have you got
planned for today?

19
00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.438
Oh, you know, the usual.

20
00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:28.999
Monsters?
Of course.

21
00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.430
You think you can work in
a fire-breathing chicken?

22
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.559
The chicken again?

23
00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.318
The chicken is funny.

24
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.278
A touch of comedy to balance
the whole thing out.

25
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:41.636
They're gonna be throwing money at you.
I just know it.

26
00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.711
Uh, they'll throw something at you.
I don't know.

27
00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.075
Okay, I'll see what I can do.

28
00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:49.436
And do you plan on finishing the
story this time, young man?

29
00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.435
If you must blink,
do it now.

30
00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:09.800
Yay!

31
00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.670
Pay careful attention to
everything you see and hear,

32
00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.990
no matter how unusual
it may seem.

33
00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.032
And please be warned,

34
00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.998
if you fidget,
if you look away,

35
00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.150
if you forget any part
of what I tell you,

36
00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.958
even for an instant,

37
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.434
then our hero
will surely perish.

38
00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:41.155
Hanzo was a mighty samurai,
but he was alone.

39
00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.755
His family taken from him,
his kingdom in ruins,

40
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.118
and his army destroyed
by the dreaded Moon King.

41
00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.633
You may recall,

42
00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.916
Hanzo was roaming
the distant Far Lands

43
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.230
in search of
a magical suit of armor.

44
00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.276
The only weapon
in the whole world

45
00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.954
that could protect him from
the power of the Moon King.

46
00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:03.112
This armor was
made up of three pieces.

47
00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.270
The first...
Oh! I know! I know!

48
00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.759
The sword unbreakable.

49
00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.239
The second...

50
00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.834
The breastplate...

51
00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.239
Impenetrable.

52
00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.639
Impenetra-bubble!

53
00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.073
Yeah!

54
00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.949
And finally,
the third weapon,

55
00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.553
the final piece
of the armor...

56
00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.915
I know this one. Pick me!

57
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.309
The helmet invulnerable!

58
00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.911
Before Hanzo
could claim the armor

59
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.072
and unite the pieces
to reveal their true power,

60
00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.469
he was attacked by
the Moon King's beast.

61
00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.154
Oh, yes!

62
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.517
Kill the chicken!
Rip it to pieces.

63
00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:07.833
Oh, my.

64
00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.309
Hanzo was filled with rage.

65
00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.594
His soul tormented

66
00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:33.240
by the grief of
a family stolen from him!

67
00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:43.033
At last, our hero was
face-to-face with his nemesis,

68
00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.269
the Moon King.

69
00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.391
So, be sure to
come back tomorrow.

70
00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:02.439
What? Oh, come on!

71
00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.748
People like an ending.

72
00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.873
Where are you going?

73
00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.758
No, you can't...
You can't leave!

74
00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:27.669
Kubo.

75
00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.311
- Kubo.
- Yes, Mother.

76
00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.434
I'm here.

77
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:36.794
Hungry?

78
00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.595
And even though
he could barely see

79
00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:43.717
his own hand in
front of his face,

80
00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:46.799
Hanzo and his
army of loyal samurai

81
00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.757
pressed on
through the blizzard.

82
00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.755
And suddenly, as quickly
as it had started,

83
00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.634
the storm cleared
before him.

84
00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.952
Hanzo breathed a sigh of relief,
for he was home.

85
00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.189
His fortress?

86
00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:05.793
The Beetle Clan castle!
Yes.

87
00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:08.189
At the very edge
of the Far Lands,

88
00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:11.192
hidden from the Moon King
by powerful magic.

89
00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.189
And then what happened,
when he got to the castle?

90
00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.108
When who got
to the castle?

91
00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.713
Hanzo! My father!

92
00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:22.637
Hanzo...
Hanzo was at the castle?

93
00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.112
He...

94
00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.193
Just give me
a second. I'm...

95
00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.557
No.

96
00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.200
It's gone. I can't...

97
00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.469
I'm sorry, Kubo.

98
00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:40.670
Perhaps I could recall
a different story.

99
00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.275
Mother, what was
Father like?

100
00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.075
Oh.

101
00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.390
This one is easy.

102
00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.996
Hanzo was a mighty warrior,
skilled with sword and bow.

103
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.958
No, what was he
really like?

104
00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.430
When he wasn't fighting,
when he was with us.

105
00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.115
He was just like you.

106
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.592
Like me?
Yes.

107
00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.992
Strong, and clever,
and funny,

108
00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.873
and, oh, so handsome.

109
00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.349
Ugh. Mother.
Come on!

110
00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:22.077
Never forget how much
he loved you, Kubo.

111
00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:24.879
He died protecting us.

112
00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:28.958
Did the Moon King...
Uh.

113
00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.393
Your grandfather.

114
00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:34.037
Did Grandfather and your
sisters really kill my father?

115
00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.872
It can't be true, can it?

116
00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:37.075
They're family.

117
00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.037
No, they are monsters.

118
00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.396
Grandfather and my sisters
stole your eye, Kubo.

119
00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.313
They must never
find you again. Never!

120
00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.710
You must always stay hidden
from the night sky,

121
00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.949
or they will find you

122
00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.871
and they'll take
you away from me.

123
00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:54.157
Promise me you will
never let this happen.

124
00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.037
Promise me, Kubo!

125
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.718
Don't be sad, Kubo.

126
00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.796
Kubo?

127
00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.758
Remember what you must do,
Kubo?

128
00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.515
Remember?

129
00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.359
Keep you with me
at all times, Mr. Monkey.

130
00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:16.440
And?

131
00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:20.792
And keep Father's robe
on my back at all times.

132
00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.995
Yes, Kubo.

133
00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.118
And there's
one more thing.

134
00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:30.509
Never, ever
stay out after dark.

135
00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:32.560
Huh?

136
00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.875
Remember?

137
00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:38.274
Yes, Mr. Monkey.
Good boy.

138
00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.155
Bedtime.

139
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.360
Mother, wake up.
You're dreaming.

140
00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.590
No. Kubo.

141
00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.193
Kubo, is that you?

142
00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.952
Yes, Mother. I'm here.

143
00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.158
Kubo, what happened
to your eye?

144
00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.119
Paper boy!

145
00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:35.828
Here, here!

146
00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.033
Come on. Come on.

147
00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.311
Come sit next to me.
I got us a good spot here.

148
00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:43.113
What do you think?

149
00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:46.158
I got myself all spruced
up for the big day.

150
00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.555
Mmm.

151
00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:53.074
I do so love the festival.

152
00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.628
A time to celebrate.

153
00:17:56.920 --> 00:18:00.390
You know, it's a shame
you never stay past sundown.

154
00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:03.472
There's fireworks,
and singing, and dancing,

155
00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:06.115
and feasting, of course.

156
00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.350
But the best part of all...

157
00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.869
Do you see those
lamps and altars?

158
00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:16.159
We use those to speak to the
loved ones that left us behind.

159
00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.636
We listen to their tales,

160
00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.793
and guide their safe return
to the blissful pure land.

161
00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.916
Really?
Did you speak to someone?

162
00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.758
Yes, I did. My husband.

163
00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.072
His voice was
as clear and loud

164
00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:32.913
as the one you use
for your stories.

165
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.355
In 72 years, he never
had a thing to say.

166
00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:38.034
Now he's gone,
I can't shut him up.

167
00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.950
You have someone
you wanna talk to, huh?

168
00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.075
Very much.

169
00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.718
Well,
what's stopping you?

170
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.199
Don't I need a lamp?

171
00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:52.751
Well, I'll bet you could
make a really nice one

172
00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.310
with that paper
folding thing you do.

173
00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:58.040
You see,

174
00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:00.795
not just a pretty face, huh?

175
00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:01.915
Now, hurry along.

176
00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:05.159
Go! There's still
time before dark.

177
00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.878
Go! Get out of here.

178
00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:43.435
Place the lamp
at the altar.

179
00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.392
Very good.

180
00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:47.072
What do we
do next, Daddy?

181
00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.752
Now we pray.

182
00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.196
We ask her spirit
to honor us with its light.

183
00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:53.872
Grandma, will you
please honor...

184
00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.234
Shh.

185
00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:57.951
Softly, softly.

186
00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:19.112
Hello, Father.
I hope you're well.

187
00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.038
I mean, I know you're dead,

188
00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:24.510
but I hope
everything is okay.

189
00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:31.312
Look, it's your robe.

190
00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:34.032
Mother says
I'll grow into it.

191
00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:37.718
She says you were
a great leader

192
00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.910
who died protecting me.

193
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.434
Saving one of my eyes.

194
00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:45.512
Two would have been ideal,
but thanks anyway.

195
00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:51.633
Father, I'm worried
about Mother.

196
00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:55.076
With every day that goes by,
she drifts further away.

197
00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.235
She talks a lot
about you, but...

198
00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.430
But I just don't know.

199
00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:04.239
I don't think she remembers
what's real anymore.

200
00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:07.675
I don't know
what's real anymore.

201
00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:11.114
I just wish you were here,

202
00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:15.671
so I could talk
to you, see you,

203
00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:17.193
find out what I should do.

204
00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:19.874
Daddy, Daddy, she's here!
Grandma is here!

205
00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.633
Now it's time
for the final part.

206
00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.433
We have to help her
get back to the spirit world.

207
00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:28.193
But she just got here.

208
00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:30.510
Come on.

209
00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.919
Father? Hello?

210
00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:39.039
Anytime.

211
00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:37.713
Fine!

212
00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:40.111
I don't need you anyway.

213
00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:47.991
Kubo.

214
00:22:56.960 --> 00:22:58.234
I'm sorry.

215
00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:09.315
Kubo.

216
00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:16.715
Kubo.

217
00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:20.319
Little boy.

218
00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:22.550
What happened to your eye?

219
00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:25.916
Who are you?
How do you know my name?

220
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.309
We are your family, Kubo.

221
00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.868
Your mother's sisters.

222
00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:35.873
And we've been looking
for you for so long.

223
00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:39.830
It's so lovely
to meet you, Kubo.

224
00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:42.591
Face-to-face.

225
00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:50.395
Come, Kubo.
Come to your aunties.

226
00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:54.589
No reason to be afraid, Kubo.

227
00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:56.671
We just need
your other eye.

228
00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:00.112
Your grandfather
admires it so.

229
00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:26.549
Help! Help!

230
00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:28.639
Somebody help!

231
00:24:28.720 --> 00:24:30.631
Help! Look out!

232
00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:32.559
Run!

233
00:24:56.920 --> 00:24:59.673
We're here, Kubo.

234
00:24:59.760 --> 00:25:01.990
Your family has
come for you.

235
00:25:14.800 --> 00:25:15.869
Kubo.

236
00:25:16.360 --> 00:25:17.509
Mother.

237
00:25:24.960 --> 00:25:28.748
Kubo, you must find the armor.
It's your only chance.

238
00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:30.188
Remember this.

239
00:25:37.640 --> 00:25:42.156
Mother! Mother! No!

240
00:25:44.600 --> 00:25:45.600
Mother!

241
00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:00.799
Kubo.

242
00:26:02.480 --> 00:26:03.480
Kubo!

243
00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:07.948
Can you hear me, Kubo?

244
00:26:12.400 --> 00:26:14.789
I said your mother
is gone.

245
00:26:14.880 --> 00:26:17.838
Your village is destroyed.
Burned to the ground.

246
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:20.991
We landed here
in the Far Lands.

247
00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:22.918
Your enemies
aren't far behind.

248
00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:26.990
We must search for shelter
before your grandfather comes.

249
00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:35.031
We need to go now.

250
00:26:36.840 --> 00:26:38.990
Come on,
get up, let's go.

251
00:27:16.200 --> 00:27:17.679
Once we're inside,

252
00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:21.150
you might be tempted
to complain about the odor.

253
00:27:25.440 --> 00:27:27.635
Keep in mind
my sense of smell

254
00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:30.393
is 10 times
stronger than yours.

255
00:28:08.200 --> 00:28:09.997
You have questions,
I can tell.

256
00:28:10.440 --> 00:28:11.953
Who...
You get three.

257
00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:15.557
I think I have more.

258
00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:18.235
Three, but first
you're gonna eat.

259
00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:20.238
Why only three?

260
00:28:20.400 --> 00:28:21.616
Okay, that was your first question.
What?

261
00:28:21.640 --> 00:28:23.040
I don't understand
what's happening!

262
00:28:23.560 --> 00:28:24.959
Who are you?

263
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:27.712
You don't recognize me?

264
00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:34.313
All these years,
you had to keep me in your pack.

265
00:28:34.440 --> 00:28:35.634
Well, now you know why.

266
00:28:35.720 --> 00:28:37.711
But you were a wooden charm.

267
00:28:37.800 --> 00:28:40.598
You were this big.

268
00:28:40.680 --> 00:28:43.752
I called that charm
"Mr. Monkey."

269
00:28:43.960 --> 00:28:45.216
And if I were
alive at that point,

270
00:28:45.240 --> 00:28:46.719
I might have
found that insulting.

271
00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:50.554
Look, your mother used the
last of her magic to save you

272
00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:52.198
and bring me to life.

273
00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:04.593
Here. Drink.

274
00:29:09.240 --> 00:29:12.152
It smells.
Everything in here smells.

275
00:29:12.240 --> 00:29:13.559
Drink it.
I don't want it.

276
00:29:13.640 --> 00:29:15.835
I said drink it.

277
00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:17.752
You're a mean monkey,
aren't you?

278
00:29:17.840 --> 00:29:20.308
Yes. Yes, I am.
And that's three.

279
00:29:20.400 --> 00:29:22.311
You're out of questions now,
so just listen.

280
00:29:22.520 --> 00:29:24.317
I'm here
to protect you, Kubo.

281
00:29:24.400 --> 00:29:26.755
And that means
you have to do as I say.

282
00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:29.195
So, if you don't eat,
you'll be weak.

283
00:29:29.280 --> 00:29:30.872
If you're weak,
you'll be slow.

284
00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:32.632
If you're slow, you'll die.

285
00:29:38.120 --> 00:29:39.519
It's too hot!

286
00:29:45.920 --> 00:29:46.920
Drink.

287
00:29:56.480 --> 00:29:57.959
Oh, excuse me.

288
00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:14.079
Okay, you better start
taking this seriously, Kubo.

289
00:30:14.160 --> 00:30:16.594
This is real.
This is not a story.

290
00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:20.634
Those things, your aunts,
they never get hungry.

291
00:30:20.720 --> 00:30:21.835
They never sleep.

292
00:30:21.920 --> 00:30:23.399
They will find you!

293
00:30:24.560 --> 00:30:26.915
And if we're not prepared,

294
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:30.231
they'll kill me
and take your other eye.

295
00:30:34.400 --> 00:30:35.594
What are we gonna do?

296
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:38.275
We're going to
find the armor.

297
00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:40.715
It's the only thing
that can protect you.

298
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:44.072
So it's real. Really real.

299
00:30:56.720 --> 00:30:58.995
Don't worry.
I'm not going to keep it.

300
00:31:00.960 --> 00:31:02.678
I pulled that
from her head.

301
00:31:03.560 --> 00:31:04.709
I didn't mean to.

302
00:31:05.080 --> 00:31:07.548
Your mother
was very powerful.

303
00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:08.993
She blessed your robes

304
00:31:09.160 --> 00:31:12.516
so that when the need was most,
they would fly you away.

305
00:31:12.640 --> 00:31:15.791
She used the last of that
power to bring me to life.

306
00:31:16.160 --> 00:31:19.470
This bracelet,
her hair, it's a memory.

307
00:31:19.560 --> 00:31:22.074
And memories are
powerful things, Kubo.

308
00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:23.754
Never lose it.

309
00:31:28.800 --> 00:31:29.949
One more question?

310
00:31:30.800 --> 00:31:31.949
Last one.

311
00:31:32.040 --> 00:31:33.473
Do you know where it is?

312
00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:35.154
The armor?

313
00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:38.314
No. No, I don't.

314
00:31:42.840 --> 00:31:44.637
Now, go to sleep.

315
00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:54.478
Goodnight, Monkey.

316
00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:13.240
Kubo.

317
00:32:14.680 --> 00:32:16.113
Kubo.

318
00:32:16.200 --> 00:32:17.918
You were
talking in your sleep.

319
00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:22.119
You were dreaming,
calling out to your father,

320
00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:26.159
and then the paper flew out of
your bag and folded itself into

321
00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:27.240
him.

322
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:35.028
He's been standing there for hours,
quietly judging us.

323
00:32:39.280 --> 00:32:41.953
I'm not even convinced
this counts as origami.

324
00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:46.034
I could swear
scissors were involved.

325
00:32:46.720 --> 00:32:47.720
Ow.

326
00:32:48.520 --> 00:32:52.274
Back home in the cave,
my mother's dreams did this,

327
00:32:52.360 --> 00:32:55.989
and the paper always
unfolded itself by morning.

328
00:33:06.040 --> 00:33:07.678
What's that about?

329
00:33:22.120 --> 00:33:23.633
What are you doing?

330
00:33:29.080 --> 00:33:32.311
I guess this is how my
father answered me. Hmm.

331
00:33:32.640 --> 00:33:34.915
I'm tempted to say
that entrusting our fate

332
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:38.436
to the guidance
of a small paper man

333
00:33:38.520 --> 00:33:39.953
seems like a bad idea.

334
00:33:40.720 --> 00:33:43.553
But it's the best
bad idea we have.

335
00:35:13.760 --> 00:35:15.398
You're growing stronger.

336
00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:17.875
You might not wanna look
quite so pleased about that.

337
00:35:18.520 --> 00:35:22.035
We grow stronger, the world
grows more dangerous.

338
00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:24.476
Life has a funny way
of keeping things balanced.

339
00:35:24.600 --> 00:35:27.990
Monkey, do you ever say
anything encouraging?

340
00:35:29.360 --> 00:35:31.351
I encourage you not to die.

341
00:35:39.400 --> 00:35:41.391
"I encourage you not to die."

342
00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:05.120
Mosquitoes. Annoying.

343
00:36:28.680 --> 00:36:30.159
Wasn't me, I swear.

344
00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:35.073
Paper runs out,
as does patience.

345
00:36:35.160 --> 00:36:36.718
I didn't ask them
to do that.

346
00:36:38.520 --> 00:36:39.953
The second time.

347
00:36:40.960 --> 00:36:43.474
I didn't!
At least, not exactly.

348
00:36:43.560 --> 00:36:45.152
I mean, I felt it, but...

349
00:36:45.240 --> 00:36:47.196
Magic is not
meant to be easy.

350
00:36:47.280 --> 00:36:48.952
You need to
learn control.

351
00:36:49.040 --> 00:36:52.635
Concentrate on what you're
doing, and always remember,

352
00:36:52.800 --> 00:36:55.109
don't mess with the monkey.

353
00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:13.758
Tread carefully, Kubo.
This isn't one of your stories.

354
00:37:14.480 --> 00:37:16.311
How do you know?
Maybe it is.

355
00:37:16.400 --> 00:37:19.915
And I'm the valiant hero
and you're the mean monkey.

356
00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:21.399
Heroes come and go.

357
00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:24.756
Any moment, something terrible
could come out of nowhere and...

358
00:37:25.800 --> 00:37:27.028
Monkey!

359
00:37:27.120 --> 00:37:28.394
Kubo!

360
00:37:41.240 --> 00:37:42.798
Monkey, wait.

361
00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:45.836
He wasn't trying to hurt me.

362
00:37:46.640 --> 00:37:48.039
He just wanted...

363
00:37:48.160 --> 00:37:49.513
Hanzo.
Hanzo?

364
00:37:51.280 --> 00:37:52.280
Hanzo.

365
00:37:57.560 --> 00:37:59.198
I still think
I'm gonna stab him.

366
00:37:59.280 --> 00:38:01.510
Why must you always
assume the worst?

367
00:38:01.600 --> 00:38:05.070
Oh! Oh! Pardon me for not trusting
this giant, spiky, insect-monster

368
00:38:05.160 --> 00:38:06.275
that just kidnapped you.

369
00:38:06.360 --> 00:38:09.113
Hanzo. Yes,
I remember him.

370
00:38:09.200 --> 00:38:11.760
I think, maybe,
he was my master.

371
00:38:12.200 --> 00:38:13.713
What?
What did you say?

372
00:38:14.760 --> 00:38:17.433
We had a crest.
A samurai crest.

373
00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:27.231
Have you seen
this crest before?

374
00:38:31.600 --> 00:38:34.273
This is a miracle.

375
00:38:34.360 --> 00:38:35.998
You have our robes.

376
00:38:36.080 --> 00:38:38.913
You're wearing our robes!

377
00:38:39.600 --> 00:38:41.192
Why are you
wearing our robes?

378
00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:42.696
He doesn't have to
answer your questions.

379
00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:44.073
Anyway, who are you?

380
00:38:46.200 --> 00:38:48.509
Many years ago,
I was cursed.

381
00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:51.913
Trapped in this
cursed state.

382
00:38:53.080 --> 00:38:55.833
Cursed to wander
the Far Lands.

383
00:38:55.920 --> 00:38:58.275
Cursed or curs-ed.

384
00:38:59.040 --> 00:39:01.759
No comrades, no master.

385
00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:04.400
Not even a name
or a single memory

386
00:39:05.040 --> 00:39:07.713
of the noble warrior
I once was.

387
00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:09.950
You used to be a man?

388
00:39:10.040 --> 00:39:11.598
No, not just any man.

389
00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:13.113
A samurai.

390
00:39:13.680 --> 00:39:15.750
I mean,
I'm pretty certain.

391
00:39:16.280 --> 00:39:17.508
Look, I had the stuff.

392
00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:20.034
I mean, I'm either a samurai
or a really bad hoarder.

393
00:39:20.120 --> 00:39:24.193
Either way, inside my thorax
beats the heart of a warrior.

394
00:39:24.440 --> 00:39:28.274
If you have no memory,
how can you be certain of anything?

395
00:39:28.600 --> 00:39:30.477
Because I get flashes.

396
00:39:30.840 --> 00:39:35.118
They come about from objects
I find on my travels.

397
00:39:35.880 --> 00:39:37.518
Sometimes it's a sound.

398
00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:40.273
Or a smell.

399
00:39:40.640 --> 00:39:42.392
You must get
a lot of flashes.

400
00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:44.357
The memories, they fade.

401
00:39:44.440 --> 00:39:46.317
And all I'm left with
is the sense that I was

402
00:39:46.960 --> 00:39:49.599
once part of
something much greater.

403
00:39:50.120 --> 00:39:51.473
Monkey, can I tell him?

404
00:39:51.560 --> 00:39:53.056
I really don't think
that's a good idea.

405
00:39:53.080 --> 00:39:54.957
He has a right.
Absolutely not.

406
00:39:55.080 --> 00:39:56.672
But... I...
No "buts." No!

407
00:39:56.760 --> 00:39:58.716
What? Tell me what?
Hanzo was my father.

408
00:39:58.800 --> 00:40:00.472
Kubo!

409
00:40:00.680 --> 00:40:01.795
This is a miracle.

410
00:40:03.040 --> 00:40:04.792
I have found
the son of my master.

411
00:40:07.120 --> 00:40:09.031
Don't even.
Oh.

412
00:40:10.040 --> 00:40:13.271
Whatever brings you to these
lands, whatever your quest,

413
00:40:13.360 --> 00:40:15.430
it is now my quest, too.

414
00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:20.117
I will join you, and I will give
my life for you, if necessary.

415
00:40:20.200 --> 00:40:21.918
Wow. You will?

416
00:40:22.640 --> 00:40:25.200
What? Do you think
that's possible?

417
00:40:25.280 --> 00:40:28.590
Look, kid, I mean, I know how these
quests go. People die all the time.

418
00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:31.148
They drop like flies.
That doesn't matter.

419
00:40:31.320 --> 00:40:32.799
'Cause I have a feeling

420
00:40:32.880 --> 00:40:35.553
this is my destiny.

421
00:40:35.640 --> 00:40:37.073
No, it isn't!

422
00:40:37.160 --> 00:40:38.957
We can't trust
anything you say,

423
00:40:39.080 --> 00:40:41.548
because you can't
trust anything you say.

424
00:40:41.680 --> 00:40:44.148
We don't know anything about you.

425
00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:47.035
Monkey,
you said it yourself.

426
00:40:47.120 --> 00:40:49.429
Our quest
is a difficult one.

427
00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:54.594
A samurai, even a cursed one with
no memory, that looks like a bug,

428
00:40:54.880 --> 00:40:55.880
could be helpful.

429
00:40:55.960 --> 00:40:58.758
Yes, I am certain
I could be helpful.

430
00:40:58.840 --> 00:40:59.840
Indispensable.

431
00:40:59.880 --> 00:41:01.552
In what way?

432
00:41:09.840 --> 00:41:13.310
Firing an arrow into a wall
is hardly what I call...

433
00:41:16.760 --> 00:41:17.909
Impressive.

434
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:19.000
Oh, look at that.

435
00:41:19.080 --> 00:41:20.696
Literally, the first
time I've ever done it.

436
00:41:20.720 --> 00:41:22.392
Just tell me of our quest,

437
00:41:22.600 --> 00:41:26.752
and I will quickly demonstrate
my numerous indispensabilities.

438
00:41:27.240 --> 00:41:29.708
Well, that's kind of
a long story.

439
00:41:30.240 --> 00:41:32.629
You've got my attention.
I promise I won't even blink.

440
00:41:32.760 --> 00:41:34.637
I actually don't think
I even can blink.

441
00:41:34.760 --> 00:41:36.318
- Do I have eyelids?
- Fine.

442
00:41:36.400 --> 00:41:38.789
Walk and talk.
Hanzo has found a path.

443
00:42:01.520 --> 00:42:04.080
So, you used
to be a toy monkey.

444
00:42:04.160 --> 00:42:07.470
Kubo, I really don't see how
this part is important to our story.

445
00:42:07.600 --> 00:42:11.559
I kept her in my pocket. She was only
like this big.

446
00:42:11.640 --> 00:42:12.880
Okay, Kubo, that's enough.
Tiny.

447
00:42:12.960 --> 00:42:14.678
And she was called
"Mr. Monkey."

448
00:42:14.800 --> 00:42:17.473
I wasn't a toy.
I was a charm.

449
00:42:17.560 --> 00:42:19.790
Of course you were.

450
00:42:41.720 --> 00:42:42.994
That doesn't look good.

451
00:42:45.240 --> 00:42:46.798
Don't touch anything.

452
00:42:54.320 --> 00:42:55.594
He did it.

453
00:43:15.480 --> 00:43:16.549
Okay.

454
00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:27.028
No. No. No.

455
00:43:31.840 --> 00:43:32.875
Yes.

456
00:43:36.040 --> 00:43:37.792
Kubo, look.

457
00:43:42.880 --> 00:43:44.711
The sword unbreakable.

458
00:43:45.320 --> 00:43:47.595
It could be a trap.

459
00:43:47.680 --> 00:43:49.557
Allow me.

460
00:43:49.640 --> 00:43:52.029
What, it's not a trap
if you do it?

461
00:43:52.120 --> 00:43:54.634
Stealth is my middle name.

462
00:43:56.880 --> 00:43:58.472
You don't even
have a first name.

463
00:43:58.560 --> 00:44:00.357
Don't worry. I got this.

464
00:44:07.640 --> 00:44:10.313
The mighty
Beetle is victorious!

465
00:44:39.400 --> 00:44:40.400
I don't got this.

466
00:44:40.480 --> 00:44:41.480
I don't got this!

467
00:44:41.560 --> 00:44:43.039
Oh, for crying out loud!

468
00:44:43.440 --> 00:44:46.273
I invoke
the sword unbreakable!

469
00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:49.715
It broke.

470
00:44:49.800 --> 00:44:52.758
So, does it just
mean the handle or...

471
00:44:53.200 --> 00:44:55.475
I'm a little disappointed
with this magic sword.

472
00:44:55.560 --> 00:44:57.755
It's not the right sword,
you idiot!

473
00:45:03.480 --> 00:45:04.480
Look!

474
00:45:05.640 --> 00:45:08.108
The sword!
It's in his head.

475
00:45:08.520 --> 00:45:11.637
Hey! I've got
a bone to pick with you.

476
00:45:11.720 --> 00:45:14.712
See, because
he's made of bones.

477
00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:16.279
You're an embarrassment.

478
00:45:17.920 --> 00:45:18.955
Uh...

479
00:45:19.360 --> 00:45:20.713
This is problematic.

480
00:45:29.960 --> 00:45:31.473
Enough with the arrows!

481
00:46:05.280 --> 00:46:06.280
Oh, foot!

482
00:46:10.360 --> 00:46:11.395
You can fly?

483
00:46:11.480 --> 00:46:13.038
Apparently, yes!

484
00:46:39.040 --> 00:46:41.634
Are you sure it isn't
the sword unfindable?

485
00:46:46.680 --> 00:46:47.680
I think I found it!

486
00:46:50.760 --> 00:46:53.354
A hand here. Anyone?

487
00:46:54.080 --> 00:46:55.593
Anyone else?

488
00:46:59.840 --> 00:47:00.955
Kubo!

489
00:47:14.560 --> 00:47:16.869
Kubo!
Monkey!

490
00:47:18.280 --> 00:47:19.349
Whoa!

491
00:47:19.480 --> 00:47:20.595
No!
Kubo!

492
00:47:24.080 --> 00:47:25.195
Huh.

493
00:47:36.760 --> 00:47:37.829
Yes!

494
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:41.360
Thank goodness that's over.

495
00:47:57.720 --> 00:48:01.156
Everything turning black.

496
00:48:01.240 --> 00:48:03.071
Then open your eyes.

497
00:48:04.480 --> 00:48:05.480
Oh.

498
00:48:05.880 --> 00:48:07.108
I can't feel my wings.

499
00:48:07.200 --> 00:48:09.589
You didn't even know you
had them five minutes ago.

500
00:48:09.680 --> 00:48:10.829
Stop wriggling.

501
00:48:10.920 --> 00:48:11.920
Here.

502
00:48:12.040 --> 00:48:13.075
Is that feeling better?

503
00:48:13.200 --> 00:48:14.633
Oh, yeah.
A little to the left.

504
00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:17.189
Down, just a bit.

505
00:48:17.280 --> 00:48:20.272
Right there. That's good.

506
00:48:20.360 --> 00:48:22.351
Wait, you're being
nice to me.

507
00:48:22.440 --> 00:48:24.032
Shh. Don't tell anyone.

508
00:48:24.120 --> 00:48:25.235
We did it, Beetle.

509
00:48:25.480 --> 00:48:26.754
We got the sword.

510
00:48:31.800 --> 00:48:33.916
Whoa. Put that down,
it's sharp!

511
00:48:41.680 --> 00:48:43.238
Ooh. Mmm.

512
00:48:43.320 --> 00:48:47.233
Okay, we're done here.
Get up.

513
00:48:47.360 --> 00:48:48.713
We have a lot
of walking to do.

514
00:48:48.800 --> 00:48:49.949
You can't be serious.

515
00:48:50.320 --> 00:48:52.072
I'm always serious.

516
00:48:52.520 --> 00:48:54.909
Are you two going
to fight, again?

517
00:48:55.000 --> 00:48:57.468
Of course not. We're having
a grown-up conversation.

518
00:48:57.560 --> 00:48:58.675
You're going to
fight again.

519
00:48:58.760 --> 00:49:01.035
Kubo, just go over there
and play with something.

520
00:49:01.120 --> 00:49:02.712
Not that!

521
00:49:02.800 --> 00:49:06.156
Monkey, this is
the Long Lake.

522
00:49:06.240 --> 00:49:08.390
We can't walk around it.

523
00:49:08.480 --> 00:49:09.840
We need to swim across.

524
00:49:10.280 --> 00:49:11.872
I can carry Kubo.

525
00:49:11.960 --> 00:49:14.474
"Carry Kubo."
That's your better idea?

526
00:49:14.560 --> 00:49:16.949
Look, I appreciate
your help. I really do.

527
00:49:17.040 --> 00:49:18.632
But when it comes
to the boy,

528
00:49:18.720 --> 00:49:20.096
I know what's best.
Oh, is that right?

529
00:49:20.120 --> 00:49:23.954
And what's best is not to be fielding
ideas from a talking cockroach.

530
00:49:24.040 --> 00:49:25.712
This coming from
a talking monkey.

531
00:49:25.800 --> 00:49:27.472
I can still
hear you, you know.

532
00:49:27.560 --> 00:49:29.232
Then play louder.

533
00:49:29.520 --> 00:49:32.016
This conversation is over.
Monkeys don't swim.

534
00:49:32.040 --> 00:49:34.793
- Not to worry. Monkey see, monkey do.
- Oh.

535
00:49:34.880 --> 00:49:36.576
How long have you
been waiting to say that?

536
00:49:36.600 --> 00:49:38.113
Ever since
I met you.

537
00:49:38.280 --> 00:49:40.400
Hey, what were we grown-up
conversation-ing about? Oh!

538
00:49:40.800 --> 00:49:43.519
You're ridiculous.
You're just absolutely ridiculous.

539
00:49:43.600 --> 00:49:44.600
Ridiculous!

540
00:49:44.680 --> 00:49:47.877
Crossing the lake
is a ridiculous idea.

541
00:49:47.960 --> 00:49:51.191
It's not your fault. There's
no sense left in your head.

542
00:49:51.280 --> 00:49:52.395
I think I resent that.

543
00:49:52.440 --> 00:49:54.510
I may not know everything...

544
00:49:54.600 --> 00:49:56.033
Anything.
Anything.

545
00:49:56.120 --> 00:49:59.192
But I do know Kubo is more
capable than you think he is.

546
00:49:59.280 --> 00:50:02.317
You're being a tiny
bit overprotective here.

547
00:50:02.400 --> 00:50:04.152
I'm being a lot
overprotective here.

548
00:50:04.240 --> 00:50:07.869
It's my job to make sure Kubo is safe,
and that is not safe.

549
00:50:07.960 --> 00:50:10.030
You... You are not safe.

550
00:50:10.120 --> 00:50:11.838
Kubo is just a child.

551
00:50:11.920 --> 00:50:14.753
And an incredibly gifted one.
He just saved our lives.

552
00:50:14.840 --> 00:50:20.198
Yes, he's very powerful,
but he still has much to learn!

553
00:50:20.280 --> 00:50:21.679
What?

554
00:50:25.960 --> 00:50:27.598
Well,
fast learner.

555
00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:34.112
Did you know
you could do that?

556
00:50:43.200 --> 00:50:44.428
Show off.

557
00:51:05.320 --> 00:51:08.153
Okay, now take
a deep breath.

558
00:51:09.920 --> 00:51:12.070
Clear your mind.

559
00:51:12.160 --> 00:51:14.230
Guess I got that part covered.

560
00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:18.199
Now, draw back slowly.
That's it.

561
00:51:18.280 --> 00:51:21.795
Close one eye. Guess you
got that part covered.

562
00:51:22.360 --> 00:51:25.636
Concentrate on what is
directly in front of you.

563
00:51:25.720 --> 00:51:28.188
Let everything else
fall away.

564
00:51:28.280 --> 00:51:31.317
And release!

565
00:51:32.120 --> 00:51:33.712
Yeah!

566
00:51:33.800 --> 00:51:36.189
Perfect shot!

567
00:51:36.320 --> 00:51:37.548
Not bad.

568
00:51:37.640 --> 00:51:39.840
And what's your plan for getting
the fish into the boat,

569
00:51:39.920 --> 00:51:41.353
so we can actually eat it?

570
00:51:45.920 --> 00:51:50.038
Well, I said I was teaching
him how to shoot, not fish.

571
00:51:50.120 --> 00:51:52.509
Fishing is
tomorrow's lesson.

572
00:51:52.880 --> 00:51:54.279
Give me that.
Whoa.

573
00:51:54.680 --> 00:51:55.874
Grabby monkey.

574
00:51:58.160 --> 00:51:59.275
Now try it.

575
00:52:01.960 --> 00:52:04.190
Pull back and...

576
00:52:06.880 --> 00:52:08.029
Whoo-hoo!

577
00:52:08.800 --> 00:52:10.313
A rope.

578
00:52:10.400 --> 00:52:11.628
It's a pretty good idea.

579
00:52:11.720 --> 00:52:13.915
Hmm. And you're not
an awful shot.

580
00:52:17.160 --> 00:52:19.469
Okay, now you two
are being weird.

581
00:52:21.360 --> 00:52:22.588
Um...

582
00:52:22.680 --> 00:52:25.148
We're going to need
something to cut this with.

583
00:52:34.720 --> 00:52:36.392
Sword unbreakable.

584
00:52:55.320 --> 00:52:57.436
Must you play
with your food?

585
00:53:00.040 --> 00:53:01.268
Yes.

586
00:53:05.600 --> 00:53:06.794
What's the matter, Kubo?

587
00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:09.395
You act like you've
never had a meal

588
00:53:09.480 --> 00:53:11.675
sitting between a monkey
and a beetle before.

589
00:53:12.800 --> 00:53:15.997
I've never had a meal sitting
between anyone before.

590
00:53:16.080 --> 00:53:18.469
Come on, eat.
You need energy.

591
00:53:18.560 --> 00:53:20.596
And this is much better
than whale soup.

592
00:53:20.680 --> 00:53:23.114
Kubo, question.

593
00:53:23.600 --> 00:53:27.752
Before you started on your heroic
quest, what were you like?

594
00:53:28.840 --> 00:53:32.230
Well, I looked
after my mother mostly.

595
00:53:32.320 --> 00:53:34.356
And I told stories

596
00:53:34.480 --> 00:53:36.755
about mighty
warriors seeking revenge

597
00:53:36.840 --> 00:53:40.196
with battles, and monsters,
and magic.

598
00:53:40.320 --> 00:53:42.151
I was pretty good
at telling them.

599
00:53:43.120 --> 00:53:44.633
Not so good
at ending them.

600
00:53:45.520 --> 00:53:49.399
Sometimes I would tell my mother
stories about little things.

601
00:53:49.480 --> 00:53:52.233
Like skimming
rocks across the river

602
00:53:52.320 --> 00:53:55.551
or catching fireflies
in the mulberry fields.

603
00:53:55.640 --> 00:53:57.232
And when I told
those stories,

604
00:53:57.320 --> 00:53:59.754
I could see her eyes
were mostly clear.

605
00:54:00.320 --> 00:54:02.038
I could tell she saw me.

606
00:54:02.560 --> 00:54:04.278
Really saw me.

607
00:54:05.120 --> 00:54:06.872
I could see her, too.

608
00:54:06.960 --> 00:54:08.359
Her real self.

609
00:54:08.440 --> 00:54:12.228
Her spirit trying
to fight its way out.

610
00:54:13.760 --> 00:54:15.079
It was beautiful.

611
00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:21.159
You know something, Kubo?

612
00:54:21.600 --> 00:54:23.750
Back when you
just told stories,

613
00:54:23.840 --> 00:54:26.229
before you went on
this great adventure,

614
00:54:26.480 --> 00:54:28.835
you were still
very much a hero.

615
00:54:49.040 --> 00:54:50.678
We're gonna have
to head for shore.

616
00:54:50.760 --> 00:54:52.796
Find a hiding place and...

617
00:55:00.960 --> 00:55:02.712
The second piece
of armor.

618
00:55:02.800 --> 00:55:04.028
The breastplate.

619
00:55:04.120 --> 00:55:06.156
It's down there?

620
00:55:06.280 --> 00:55:07.508
Okay, I got it.

621
00:55:07.600 --> 00:55:09.591
Beetle, wait!
No, don't worry.

622
00:55:09.680 --> 00:55:13.309
Beetles can hold their breath
under water for a very long time.

623
00:55:13.400 --> 00:55:14.469
What? Since when?

624
00:55:14.560 --> 00:55:16.152
It's a well-known fact,
Monkey.

625
00:55:16.240 --> 00:55:18.800
So, you don't remember anything
at all, but beetles swimming?

626
00:55:18.880 --> 00:55:20.313
That's what
sticks in there?

627
00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:21.400
No, Beetle.

628
00:55:21.440 --> 00:55:24.318
My mother told me
a story about the Long Lake.

629
00:55:24.400 --> 00:55:26.152
There's something
under the water.

630
00:55:26.240 --> 00:55:27.240
Oh, yeah?

631
00:55:27.480 --> 00:55:28.833
Um...

632
00:55:29.160 --> 00:55:30.991
What kind of something?

633
00:55:31.080 --> 00:55:33.150
She said there was
a garden of eyes,

634
00:55:33.240 --> 00:55:36.676
eyes that stare into you,
into your soul.

635
00:55:36.760 --> 00:55:40.912
They show you secrets, things to
keep you down there with them.

636
00:55:41.600 --> 00:55:42.635
Forever.

637
00:55:43.520 --> 00:55:44.873
Okay.

638
00:55:45.240 --> 00:55:48.232
Well, I won't look
directly into anyone's eyes,

639
00:55:48.320 --> 00:55:50.595
even if I'm being
incredibly sincere.

640
00:55:52.240 --> 00:55:53.514
You're gonna miss me, Monkey.

641
00:56:03.320 --> 00:56:04.469
Be careful.

642
00:56:31.520 --> 00:56:35.832
He's searching for the armor
just like his insolent father.

643
00:56:35.920 --> 00:56:37.638
Yes, sister.

644
00:56:37.720 --> 00:56:42.157
Then we must ensure he does
not find what remains.

645
00:56:53.800 --> 00:56:55.791
Monkey,
I think he's in trouble!

646
00:56:56.480 --> 00:56:57.674
We should help him.

647
00:56:57.760 --> 00:57:00.752
Kubo, your aunts are still out there.
I'm sorry.

648
00:57:00.840 --> 00:57:02.990
But we have to head for shore.

649
00:57:03.960 --> 00:57:05.109
Kubo!

650
00:57:11.520 --> 00:57:12.520
Kubo.

651
00:57:14.920 --> 00:57:16.273
Look at this.

652
00:57:16.640 --> 00:57:21.270
I come fishing and all I
reel in is a stinking ape.

653
00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:25.072
How pathetic that
this filthy creature

654
00:57:25.160 --> 00:57:27.469
is all that's left
of my sister's magic.

655
00:57:27.840 --> 00:57:31.150
This filthy creature
will tear you apart!

656
00:58:06.560 --> 00:58:08.039
Kubo.

657
00:58:23.920 --> 00:58:25.069
Kubo?

658
00:58:27.280 --> 00:58:31.717
I have crushed creatures who could
fit this world on their fingernail.

659
00:58:32.320 --> 00:58:34.390
This victory
brings me no honor.

660
00:58:38.240 --> 00:58:41.198
Imagine how you're going
to feel when you lose.

661
00:58:44.400 --> 00:58:46.391
I felt loss only once.

662
00:58:47.280 --> 00:58:49.953
Eleven years ago,
I lost my sister.

663
00:58:52.240 --> 00:58:55.915
She fell in love with a fool
and betrayed our father!

664
00:58:58.800 --> 00:59:00.791
She was an
ungrateful coward!

665
00:59:11.880 --> 00:59:13.916
Who's the coward now?

666
00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:28.436
I got it! I got it!

667
00:59:30.760 --> 00:59:34.070
Beetle, what happened?
Where's Kubo?

668
00:59:34.320 --> 00:59:35.878
Um...

669
00:59:42.960 --> 00:59:44.154
Uh-oh.

670
00:59:54.040 --> 00:59:56.634
Get back down there!
He's in trouble!

671
00:59:57.160 --> 00:59:58.957
I got it.

672
01:00:11.760 --> 01:00:13.318
Mother. Mother.

673
01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:15.274
Mother. Mother.

674
01:00:15.360 --> 01:00:18.238
Mother.

675
01:00:48.320 --> 01:00:49.992
It never fails to amaze me

676
01:00:50.080 --> 01:00:54.710
how the creatures down here fight
so hard just to die another day.

677
01:00:54.800 --> 01:00:57.712
Down here, there are
days worth fighting for.

678
01:00:59.360 --> 01:01:01.237
There is nothing down
here worth anything!

679
01:01:08.680 --> 01:01:11.240
It's pathetic what
happened to my sister.

680
01:01:11.320 --> 01:01:14.232
I looked up to her.
She was so strong.

681
01:01:15.080 --> 01:01:17.640
And love made her weak.

682
01:01:17.720 --> 01:01:18.720
No!

683
01:01:20.280 --> 01:01:21.599
It made me stronger.

684
01:01:38.880 --> 01:01:39.880
Over here.

685
01:01:41.600 --> 01:01:42.953
The eyes...

686
01:01:43.760 --> 01:01:44.954
It was the eyes.

687
01:01:45.920 --> 01:01:47.273
They had him in a trance.

688
01:01:47.720 --> 01:01:49.039
Oh, no.

689
01:01:49.120 --> 01:01:50.553
No.

690
01:01:50.640 --> 01:01:53.154
Come on. Come on, Kubo.

691
01:01:53.240 --> 01:01:56.391
Wake up. Please wake up!

692
01:01:58.680 --> 01:02:01.592
Please, please wake up.

693
01:02:02.480 --> 01:02:04.118
It's gonna be all right.

694
01:02:04.920 --> 01:02:06.592
It's gonna be all right.

695
01:02:07.200 --> 01:02:08.269
I'm here.

696
01:02:09.480 --> 01:02:10.833
I'm right here.

697
01:02:34.320 --> 01:02:35.320
I saw...

698
01:02:35.840 --> 01:02:37.432
What? What did you see?

699
01:02:37.840 --> 01:02:38.989
I saw...

700
01:02:41.440 --> 01:02:42.475
Mother.

701
01:02:43.520 --> 01:02:44.714
My son.

702
01:02:58.600 --> 01:03:01.433
So, you must look
more like your dad, then?

703
01:03:05.360 --> 01:03:06.759
You're staring.

704
01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:10.468
Let me guess.
You have questions.

705
01:03:11.360 --> 01:03:12.952
Why...
I'll start.

706
01:03:13.040 --> 01:03:16.669
First question. If I'm
Beetle and you're Monkey,

707
01:03:16.760 --> 01:03:18.352
why isn't he called "Boy"?

708
01:03:20.560 --> 01:03:21.709
Oh, boy.

709
01:03:23.200 --> 01:03:24.918
Questions can wait.

710
01:03:25.480 --> 01:03:26.629
We need sleep.

711
01:03:26.720 --> 01:03:29.712
Tell us your story,
then we can sleep.

712
01:03:30.560 --> 01:03:31.629
Please?

713
01:03:33.040 --> 01:03:34.075
Okay.

714
01:03:34.680 --> 01:03:36.238
Perhaps you can help me.

715
01:03:44.280 --> 01:03:46.589
The night I met
your father...

716
01:03:50.760 --> 01:03:51.954
Mother.

717
01:03:55.760 --> 01:04:00.993
My sisters and I went to the
Temple of Bones to kill Hanzo.

718
01:04:06.440 --> 01:04:07.555
Oh, right.

719
01:04:15.280 --> 01:04:17.236
At the bidding
of the Moon King,

720
01:04:17.320 --> 01:04:20.118
my sisters and I had come
down from the night sky

721
01:04:20.200 --> 01:04:22.395
and killed many
noble warriors.

722
01:04:23.040 --> 01:04:25.349
Your grandfather told us

723
01:04:25.440 --> 01:04:28.113
that any man who
found the magical armor

724
01:04:28.400 --> 01:04:29.879
would grow too powerful

725
01:04:29.960 --> 01:04:31.871
and be a threat
to the heavens.

726
01:04:32.440 --> 01:04:36.194
That night, I arrived at
the temple before my sisters.

727
01:04:37.840 --> 01:04:41.469
And there he was,
the mighty Hanzo.

728
01:04:44.680 --> 01:04:47.319
"You have offended
my father," I told him.

729
01:04:47.760 --> 01:04:49.478
"Now you must die."

730
01:04:49.560 --> 01:04:51.949
Yeah, that's so you.

731
01:04:52.040 --> 01:04:53.871
Beetle. Shh!

732
01:04:54.760 --> 01:04:56.113
We fought.

733
01:05:01.360 --> 01:05:02.793
Hanzo was strong.

734
01:05:04.000 --> 01:05:05.319
But then he stopped.

735
01:05:06.120 --> 01:05:09.430
He looked into my eyes and
uttered four simple words.

736
01:05:10.640 --> 01:05:12.756
These words
changed everything.

737
01:05:13.720 --> 01:05:17.269
"I love you,

738
01:05:18.040 --> 01:05:19.393
"Monkey"?

739
01:05:21.520 --> 01:05:23.875
"You are my quest,"

740
01:05:23.960 --> 01:05:25.188
he whispered.

741
01:05:25.760 --> 01:05:28.069
I had seen the wonders
of the universe,

742
01:05:28.160 --> 01:05:31.994
but the warmth of his gaze
as I looked into his eyes...

743
01:05:33.000 --> 01:05:36.675
That...
That I had never known.

744
01:05:36.920 --> 01:05:39.275
It was his humanity I saw.

745
01:05:39.360 --> 01:05:41.271
And it was more powerful
than anything

746
01:05:41.360 --> 01:05:43.191
in my cold realm.

747
01:05:44.040 --> 01:05:46.759
In recognizing
his compassion,

748
01:05:46.880 --> 01:05:48.518
I recognized my own.

749
01:05:49.320 --> 01:05:50.878
I spared his life.

750
01:05:51.480 --> 01:05:53.038
He gave me mine.

751
01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:56.913
And...
And then he gave me you.

752
01:05:58.200 --> 01:06:00.111
But your grandfather
found us.

753
01:06:01.080 --> 01:06:04.629
His rage at my betrayal
shook the heavens.

754
01:06:10.080 --> 01:06:13.550
Your father and his army
gave their lives,

755
01:06:13.640 --> 01:06:16.393
allowing me to escape
with you in my arms.

756
01:06:19.920 --> 01:06:22.593
Why does Grandfather
hate me?

757
01:06:23.400 --> 01:06:24.674
Oh, Kubo...

758
01:06:26.040 --> 01:06:27.519
He doesn't hate you.

759
01:06:28.240 --> 01:06:31.232
He wants to make
you just like him.

760
01:06:31.320 --> 01:06:32.992
Blind to humanity,

761
01:06:34.400 --> 01:06:35.992
as I once was.

762
01:06:36.560 --> 01:06:38.710
Only then can you take
your place beside him

763
01:06:38.800 --> 01:06:40.472
as part of his family.

764
01:06:41.080 --> 01:06:43.116
Cold and hard.

765
01:06:44.640 --> 01:06:46.039
And perfect.

766
01:06:47.440 --> 01:06:49.954
I'll never be like him,
never.

767
01:06:52.920 --> 01:06:54.148
I know.

768
01:07:05.280 --> 01:07:06.554
He's exhausted.

769
01:07:06.640 --> 01:07:07.640
Mmm.

770
01:07:08.640 --> 01:07:09.640
Me, too.

771
01:07:09.720 --> 01:07:11.438
I'm not tucking you in.

772
01:07:15.960 --> 01:07:17.029
You're hurt.

773
01:07:18.680 --> 01:07:20.113
It's just a scratch.

774
01:07:22.440 --> 01:07:27.912
Monkey, why didn't you tell him
sooner who you really are?

775
01:07:29.760 --> 01:07:34.117
The magic that keeps
me here, it's fading.

776
01:07:35.400 --> 01:07:36.958
Soon I'll be gone.

777
01:07:37.840 --> 01:07:40.229
And then Kubo
will be alone again.

778
01:07:40.320 --> 01:07:41.469
Not alone.

779
01:07:41.880 --> 01:07:44.269
He is the son of Hanzo.

780
01:07:44.360 --> 01:07:47.796
I will do everything I can
to keep him from harm.

781
01:07:48.680 --> 01:07:50.272
Thank you, Beetle.

782
01:07:50.840 --> 01:07:55.470
To know Kubo has someone to
watch over him when I'm gone.

783
01:07:57.160 --> 01:07:59.833
That would be a fine way
to end my story.

784
01:08:00.920 --> 01:08:04.310
Your story will never end.

785
01:08:04.720 --> 01:08:09.157
It will be told by him and by
the people he shares it with.

786
01:08:09.240 --> 01:08:11.356
And by the people
they share it with.

787
01:08:11.760 --> 01:08:13.990
And by the people
they share it with,

788
01:08:14.080 --> 01:08:16.310
and by the people
they share it with.

789
01:08:16.400 --> 01:08:18.038
And by the people...
Beetle.

790
01:08:18.480 --> 01:08:22.996
The point is
your story will live on

791
01:08:23.840 --> 01:08:24.989
in him.

792
01:08:55.160 --> 01:08:56.912
Hello, my young friend.

793
01:08:57.600 --> 01:08:59.670
Why don't you
join in my song?

794
01:09:00.720 --> 01:09:01.914
But how did you...

795
01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:04.588
You're...
Even blinder than you?

796
01:09:05.400 --> 01:09:07.118
Twice as much,
to be precise.

797
01:09:08.760 --> 01:09:11.718
Which means I see
double the truth.

798
01:09:12.760 --> 01:09:14.273
This is all a dream.

799
01:09:15.280 --> 01:09:17.191
Is this a good dream
or a bad one?

800
01:09:17.440 --> 01:09:19.192
See for yourself.

801
01:09:36.920 --> 01:09:38.831
My father's fortress.

802
01:09:38.920 --> 01:09:39.920
Yes.

803
01:09:47.120 --> 01:09:48.758
The last piece
of the armor.

804
01:09:49.160 --> 01:09:50.275
It's here?

805
01:09:50.920 --> 01:09:54.117
Follow the setting sun
and you'll find it,

806
01:09:54.440 --> 01:09:57.591
in the place that
might have been your home.

807
01:09:58.440 --> 01:10:01.193
Claim your birthright, Kubo.

808
01:10:02.280 --> 01:10:05.397
Give this story
a happy ending.

809
01:10:10.720 --> 01:10:12.711
Mother! Beetle! Wake up!

810
01:10:12.800 --> 01:10:14.518
I'm up. I'm up.

811
01:10:14.600 --> 01:10:16.636
Well, I'm down.

812
01:10:17.040 --> 01:10:18.075
Off.

813
01:10:18.480 --> 01:10:20.198
I think I slept
on something.

814
01:10:21.880 --> 01:10:23.472
Sword uncomfortable.

815
01:10:23.840 --> 01:10:25.876
The helmet,
I know where it is.

816
01:10:25.960 --> 01:10:27.632
I saw it in a dream, Beetle.

817
01:10:28.160 --> 01:10:29.479
A dream?

818
01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:32.714
Well, it doesn't mean
anything in particular.

819
01:10:32.800 --> 01:10:36.793
I mean, I dreamed I fought a giant
skeleton with swords in its head.

820
01:10:37.160 --> 01:10:39.230
That really happened.

821
01:10:39.320 --> 01:10:40.548
Oh, yeah.

822
01:10:40.720 --> 01:10:42.233
Beetle.

823
01:10:42.320 --> 01:10:44.231
Come on, this way.

824
01:11:21.120 --> 01:11:26.353
I spy with my one eye
something beginning with "S."

825
01:11:29.040 --> 01:11:30.359
Snow?
No.

826
01:11:32.280 --> 01:11:33.349
Snowflake?

827
01:11:33.720 --> 01:11:35.278
No.
Okay.

828
01:11:36.080 --> 01:11:37.115
Oh. Pfft.

829
01:11:37.200 --> 01:11:38.315
Snow covered trees.

830
01:11:38.400 --> 01:11:40.277
Nothing to do with snow.

831
01:11:41.040 --> 01:11:42.951
How about "serious"?

832
01:11:43.960 --> 01:11:45.154
Stupid.

833
01:11:46.200 --> 01:11:47.519
Okay, I got it.

834
01:11:47.600 --> 01:11:48.794
Snow.

835
01:11:48.880 --> 01:11:51.553
He said it wasn't "snow."

836
01:11:51.880 --> 01:11:53.313
It's a song.

837
01:11:53.400 --> 01:11:54.833
Well, that's not fair.

838
01:11:54.920 --> 01:11:56.273
How do you see a song?

839
01:11:56.360 --> 01:11:57.360
You look.

840
01:11:59.880 --> 01:12:01.393
Golden heron.

841
01:12:02.200 --> 01:12:05.078
It's believed they hold the
souls of the departed,

842
01:12:05.160 --> 01:12:07.549
carrying them over
to wherever they need to go.

843
01:12:08.400 --> 01:12:09.400
Hmm.

844
01:12:10.160 --> 01:12:11.718
What are they singing?

845
01:12:12.920 --> 01:12:14.319
It's beautiful.

846
01:12:14.480 --> 01:12:17.916
Many say the song's about
what happens when we die.

847
01:12:18.880 --> 01:12:22.111
How we don't
just disappear.

848
01:12:22.600 --> 01:12:23.669
We don't?

849
01:12:23.760 --> 01:12:26.194
Uh, so, what happens to us?

850
01:12:26.560 --> 01:12:28.676
Well, like Kubo's paper,
we shift.

851
01:12:28.760 --> 01:12:31.194
We transform so we can
continue our story

852
01:12:31.280 --> 01:12:32.554
to another place.

853
01:12:33.160 --> 01:12:37.073
The end of one story is merely
the beginning of another.

854
01:13:00.080 --> 01:13:01.957
I remember this place.

855
01:13:42.520 --> 01:13:45.318
This was where my father
prepared for his quest.

856
01:14:10.520 --> 01:14:12.954
There's something
I don't understand.

857
01:14:13.040 --> 01:14:14.837
Why would the helmet
be here?

858
01:14:19.680 --> 01:14:20.874
Kubo!

859
01:14:52.920 --> 01:14:54.148
Release us!

860
01:14:54.920 --> 01:14:56.558
Oh, sister.

861
01:14:58.240 --> 01:15:00.390
I remember how we
looked up to you.

862
01:15:01.600 --> 01:15:04.194
Of all of us,
you shone the brightest.

863
01:15:05.040 --> 01:15:06.473
Such a waste.

864
01:15:07.200 --> 01:15:11.478
All we ever wished was to be a
family in our home among the stars.

865
01:15:11.800 --> 01:15:15.076
I think we have very different
definitions of family.

866
01:15:15.160 --> 01:15:17.196
Don't you touch him,
you witch!

867
01:15:17.280 --> 01:15:18.679
And then there's you,

868
01:15:18.760 --> 01:15:22.196
the thieving insect
who stole my sister's soul.

869
01:15:22.280 --> 01:15:23.280
What?

870
01:15:25.200 --> 01:15:27.111
Oh, this is precious.

871
01:15:27.320 --> 01:15:29.231
You've been
together all this time

872
01:15:29.320 --> 01:15:31.515
and you haven't
even realized?

873
01:15:36.120 --> 01:15:38.111
You took her from us.

874
01:15:38.200 --> 01:15:40.953
It was only fitting
we took something from you.

875
01:15:41.400 --> 01:15:44.312
How swiftly those memories
spilled from your head,

876
01:15:44.400 --> 01:15:48.712
wiping out all recollection
of your obscene union.

877
01:15:48.800 --> 01:15:50.028
Hanzo.

878
01:15:50.640 --> 01:15:51.709
What?

879
01:15:52.640 --> 01:15:53.789
Hanzo?

880
01:15:55.600 --> 01:15:57.477
I... I didn't know.

881
01:16:00.680 --> 01:16:02.159
No!

882
01:16:07.480 --> 01:16:10.631
I'm forgetting
what I came here for.

883
01:16:59.320 --> 01:17:00.435
Mother!

884
01:17:17.720 --> 01:17:19.756
Shh. It's okay. I'm here.

885
01:17:20.640 --> 01:17:21.755
Father?

886
01:17:22.720 --> 01:17:23.789
My son.

887
01:17:30.120 --> 01:17:32.236
Seems I'm married to a bug.

888
01:17:33.200 --> 01:17:34.315
Yeah.

889
01:17:35.360 --> 01:17:36.873
But a samurai bug.

890
01:17:40.640 --> 01:17:42.631
You are my quest.

891
01:17:43.840 --> 01:17:45.398
You always have been.

892
01:17:47.520 --> 01:17:51.877
Hanzo, keep him safe,
no matter what.

893
01:17:54.560 --> 01:17:56.198
I promise I will.

894
01:18:05.760 --> 01:18:06.795
No!

895
01:18:09.520 --> 01:18:11.511
Fly home, Kubo.

896
01:21:07.120 --> 01:21:09.190
Kubo? Is that you?

897
01:21:12.240 --> 01:21:13.958
You have to
leave this place.

898
01:21:14.040 --> 01:21:16.474
The Moon King, he's coming.

899
01:21:30.480 --> 01:21:31.708
Grandfather!

900
01:21:32.480 --> 01:21:34.038
It's me, Kubo!

901
01:21:34.920 --> 01:21:36.797
I know you can see me!

902
01:21:39.480 --> 01:21:41.471
Hello, grandson.

903
01:21:42.200 --> 01:21:44.555
It's so good to
see you at last.

904
01:21:45.160 --> 01:21:46.639
So to speak.

905
01:21:49.120 --> 01:21:52.351
And I see you found
the armor.

906
01:21:53.640 --> 01:21:55.437
Seems your mother
had a reason

907
01:21:55.520 --> 01:21:58.193
to bring you to this
dreadful place after all.

908
01:22:03.040 --> 01:22:04.314
I see.

909
01:22:06.320 --> 01:22:07.514
I know you do.

910
01:22:08.000 --> 01:22:11.276
That's how this all began.
You finally saw me.

911
01:22:12.080 --> 01:22:15.470
It was my fault. I should've
listened to my parents.

912
01:22:17.040 --> 01:22:21.670
Kubo, we both want
the exact same thing.

913
01:22:21.760 --> 01:22:24.832
You want to take my other eye.
That's what you want!

914
01:22:25.720 --> 01:22:30.396
Well, yes. But do you
know why I want it?

915
01:22:31.240 --> 01:22:35.074
Because you're old,
and mean, and cruel.

916
01:22:35.160 --> 01:22:37.799
Oh, now,
that's a little harsh.

917
01:22:37.880 --> 01:22:42.032
As long as you cling
to that silly, useless eye,

918
01:22:42.120 --> 01:22:45.032
you can't come up
to live with me.

919
01:22:45.720 --> 01:22:47.312
In the heavens.

920
01:22:47.840 --> 01:22:52.630
You'll be stuck
down here in this hell,

921
01:22:52.720 --> 01:22:58.317
staring with that lonely eye
at hate and heartache

922
01:22:58.400 --> 01:23:02.473
and suffering and death.

923
01:23:05.760 --> 01:23:07.079
Where I want to
take you,

924
01:23:07.240 --> 01:23:10.471
we have none
of those things.

925
01:23:10.560 --> 01:23:13.836
It'll just be you
with your family.

926
01:23:14.560 --> 01:23:15.754
Where you belong.

927
01:23:15.840 --> 01:23:17.990
My family is gone.

928
01:23:18.080 --> 01:23:20.674
You killed them.
No...

929
01:23:20.760 --> 01:23:24.355
They brought their
fates upon themselves!

930
01:23:24.440 --> 01:23:29.594
They disgraced me and upset
the order of everything!

931
01:23:29.680 --> 01:23:31.750
That's how
your story goes.

932
01:23:33.640 --> 01:23:35.073
Oh, Kubo...

933
01:23:35.600 --> 01:23:40.230
When you're up there with me,
you will be beyond stories.

934
01:23:40.320 --> 01:23:44.757
You will be immortal.

935
01:23:45.200 --> 01:23:46.918
You will be

936
01:23:49.200 --> 01:23:50.918
infinite.

937
01:23:51.760 --> 01:23:55.275
No. You're wrong,
not infinite.

938
01:23:55.360 --> 01:23:57.590
All stories have an end.

939
01:23:58.160 --> 01:24:00.116
Is that right?

940
01:24:00.880 --> 01:24:04.111
And how does
this story end?

941
01:24:07.080 --> 01:24:08.672
I kill you.

942
01:24:08.760 --> 01:24:09.760
Oh.

943
01:24:10.040 --> 01:24:12.873
Very well.
Is this your wish,

944
01:24:12.960 --> 01:24:17.351
to do battle with a hideous
monster who ruined your life,

945
01:24:17.440 --> 01:24:22.150
to prove your worth
like your doomed father?

946
01:24:22.680 --> 01:24:24.477
How mortal.

947
01:25:44.560 --> 01:25:47.199
You want to be human?

948
01:25:47.480 --> 01:25:51.268
Then share their weakness!

949
01:25:52.400 --> 01:25:55.710
Suffer their humiliation!

950
01:25:57.400 --> 01:25:59.550
Feel their pain!

951
01:26:43.280 --> 01:26:47.193
This is the end
of your story.

952
01:26:47.440 --> 01:26:51.956
Now, take one last
look with that lonely eye,

953
01:26:52.040 --> 01:26:58.559
one last look at this
wretched place you call home.

954
01:26:59.960 --> 01:27:01.837
I'm not leaving.

955
01:27:02.600 --> 01:27:04.431
For every horrible thing
down here,

956
01:27:05.320 --> 01:27:07.390
there's something
far more beautiful.

957
01:27:07.880 --> 01:27:09.677
My mother saw it.

958
01:27:09.760 --> 01:27:12.149
So did my father. I see it.

959
01:27:12.440 --> 01:27:14.237
Even with just one eye.

960
01:27:14.400 --> 01:27:18.632
Then I'll just have to rip
it out of your head again,

961
01:27:18.920 --> 01:27:20.148
won't I?

962
01:27:23.120 --> 01:27:25.680
If you must blink,
do it now.

963
01:27:29.840 --> 01:27:31.956
I know why
you want my eye.

964
01:27:32.680 --> 01:27:33.954
Because without it,

965
01:27:34.040 --> 01:27:37.316
I can't look into the eyes of
another and see their soul.

966
01:27:37.640 --> 01:27:41.235
Their love...
Everything you loved is gone!

967
01:27:42.000 --> 01:27:45.470
Everything you knew
has been taken from you!

968
01:27:45.560 --> 01:27:46.754
No.

969
01:27:46.840 --> 01:27:48.273
It's in my memories.

970
01:27:48.360 --> 01:27:50.749
The most powerful
kind of magic there is.

971
01:28:03.880 --> 01:28:06.553
It makes us stronger
than you'll ever be.

972
01:28:09.520 --> 01:28:13.479
These are the memories of
those we have loved and lost.

973
01:28:14.040 --> 01:28:17.191
And if we hold their stories
deep in our hearts,

974
01:28:17.720 --> 01:28:20.632
then you will never
take them away from us.

975
01:28:33.360 --> 01:28:35.351
And that really
is the least of it.

976
01:28:55.320 --> 01:28:56.958
Where am I?

977
01:28:57.040 --> 01:28:59.190
Hello, Grandfather.

978
01:28:59.760 --> 01:29:00.954
Oh, hello.

979
01:29:03.080 --> 01:29:05.116
What happened to your eye?

980
01:29:05.600 --> 01:29:06.919
Don't you remember?

981
01:29:07.720 --> 01:29:11.156
No, I... I'm sorry,
young man.

982
01:29:12.000 --> 01:29:14.434
But I seem to have
forgotten my story.

983
01:29:16.000 --> 01:29:17.592
Can you help me?

984
01:29:19.560 --> 01:29:20.993
I'll tell him.

985
01:29:21.080 --> 01:29:22.718
No, we'll all tell him.

986
01:29:22.800 --> 01:29:25.553
We'll tell him
everything he needs to know.

987
01:29:26.440 --> 01:29:30.592
You are the kindest,
sweetest man

988
01:29:30.680 --> 01:29:32.477
to ever live
in this village.

989
01:29:32.560 --> 01:29:34.437
Oh. Oh, really?
Yes.

990
01:29:34.520 --> 01:29:35.714
Uh... Uh...

991
01:29:35.800 --> 01:29:38.030
Every day,
you walk around smiling

992
01:29:38.120 --> 01:29:39.872
and handing out
coins to children.

993
01:29:39.960 --> 01:29:41.029
Like me!

994
01:29:41.120 --> 01:29:42.838
And old women.

995
01:29:42.920 --> 01:29:43.920
Oh.

996
01:29:44.000 --> 01:29:46.560
You... You taught
my kids to swim.

997
01:29:46.640 --> 01:29:47.675
What?

998
01:29:47.760 --> 01:29:49.955
And you give
blankets to the poor.

999
01:29:50.040 --> 01:29:51.040
You're a good man.

1000
01:29:51.120 --> 01:29:53.634
- You fed the hungry.
- You always lend a helping hand.

1001
01:29:53.720 --> 01:29:55.915
You're a great
example.

1002
01:29:57.800 --> 01:29:59.438
It turns out
I'm pretty selfless.

1003
01:29:59.520 --> 01:30:01.158
That's why we love you.

1004
01:30:01.240 --> 01:30:05.233
You know, we have
something in common.

1005
01:30:05.320 --> 01:30:07.515
We both adore
your grandson.

1006
01:30:08.840 --> 01:30:11.195
His name is Kubo.

1007
01:30:13.440 --> 01:30:14.919
Kubo?

1008
01:30:16.440 --> 01:30:17.998
I'm sorry.

1009
01:30:19.000 --> 01:30:21.878
But I...
But I don't remember.

1010
01:30:22.680 --> 01:30:23.749
Well...

1011
01:30:24.360 --> 01:30:26.828
Your grandson's
a storyteller.

1012
01:30:27.840 --> 01:30:30.673
He'll tell you all the
stories you've forgotten.

1013
01:30:32.040 --> 01:30:33.314
Really?

1014
01:30:36.760 --> 01:30:38.113
Of course.

1015
01:31:05.800 --> 01:31:06.869
Hello, Mother.

1016
01:31:07.880 --> 01:31:08.880
Father.

1017
01:31:10.120 --> 01:31:15.274
I know my stories can tend
to get a little, um, long,

1018
01:31:15.360 --> 01:31:17.874
so I'll keep this brief.

1019
01:31:19.040 --> 01:31:22.191
I'm very grateful I've had
the chance to meet you both,

1020
01:31:22.840 --> 01:31:26.196
hear your wisdom,
feel your kindness,

1021
01:31:27.120 --> 01:31:29.475
even eat a meal
sitting between you.

1022
01:31:30.680 --> 01:31:32.557
This was a happy story.

1023
01:31:33.440 --> 01:31:37.228
But it could still be
a whole lot happier.

1024
01:31:39.200 --> 01:31:42.829
I don't know exactly
what the rules are

1025
01:31:42.920 --> 01:31:44.797
or how this works,

1026
01:31:45.400 --> 01:31:47.516
but if there
were any way to...

1027
01:31:48.360 --> 01:31:51.830
You know, I still need you.

1028
01:31:52.920 --> 01:31:56.276
So I can say this
has been a happy story,

1029
01:31:56.360 --> 01:31:57.713
or I could feel it.

1030
01:31:58.080 --> 01:31:59.911
We could all feel it.

1031
01:32:00.880 --> 01:32:02.711
Then we could
end this story.

1032
01:32:04.000 --> 01:32:05.228
Together.

1033
01:32:48.320 --> 01:32:49.389
The end.
